  <prompt>DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:53 and DataverseWebApiClient.cs:42 never read Graph:ManagedIdentity:Enabled — secret presence alone selects the secret path. On dev, where API_CLIENT_SECRET is set because OBO needs it, both run on the client secret today despite MI being enabled. Make both read the flag.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADR-028 and the Spaarke.Dataverse layering rules strictly.</role>
  <goal>Both sites select their credential from the flag, not from secret presence, with a seam test covering the full matrix.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>This is a live defect, not a hypothetical: it means dev observation of these two files currently reflects the SECRET code path, not the MI path. That matters to this project and to dataverse-access-unification-r1, whose parity testing would otherwise characterise the wrong path (see COORDINATION-DATAVERSE-ACCESS-UNIFICATION §5.1). Independently correct regardless of the credential decision.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiClient.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Auth/CredentialSelectionSeamTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="003" status="pending">Credential decision recorded</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: these two sites only. Do not change the credential TYPE here — that is Phase 2. This task only corrects which branch is selected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DataverseWebApiService.cs:65 is already correctly flag-gated by #3b — copy its gating shape, do not re-implement it differently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: Spaarke.Dataverse must gain NO ProjectReference and NO new package. CI-enforced by tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/LayerDependencyTests.cs FR-14.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: coverage goes to tests/integration/seam/**. Do NOT write DI-registration tests or ctor null-check tests — both are banned (B3/B4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DataverseWebApiClient is scheduled for DELETION by dataverse-access-unification-r1. Keep the change minimal (~6 lines); do not refactor it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse credential selection, managed identity gating</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read DataverseWebApiService.cs:60-90 to capture the correct gating shape from #3b.</step>
    <step>Apply the same gating to DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:49-77, preserving the OBO branch semantics.</step>
    <step>Apply it to DataverseWebApiClient.cs:36-54.</step>
    <step>Add a seam test asserting the selected credential type across the flag/secret matrix.</step>
    <step>Verify publish size + CVE scan per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Correcting the gating breaks OBO in DataverseAccessDataSource — the OBO branch and the app-only branch are entangled there. STOP and report; this is the highest-blast-radius file in the library.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiClient.cs</output>
    <output type="new">tests/integration/seam/Auth/CredentialSelectionSeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Flag true + secret present: both sites resolve the MI credential.</criterion>
    <criterion>Flag false + secret present: both sites resolve the secret.</criterion>
    <criterion>Flag true + no secret: both sites resolve MI.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: flag false + no secret fails fast with an actionable message, not a null credential.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: OBO in DataverseAccessDataSource still fails CLOSED (AccessRights.None) when the user lacks rights.</criterion>
    <criterion>LayerDependencyTests FR-14 passes unmodified; Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported vs the 44.96 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <completion date="2026-08-20" rigor="FULL">
      ESCALATION TRIGGER FIRED AND WAS RESOLVED BY OWNER DECISION (Option A -- decouple).

      DataverseWebApiClient: clean gating fix (no OBO path). DataverseAccessDataSource: the prescribed
      "copy DataverseWebApiService's shape" would have set _cca = null whenever MI is enabled, disabling OBO and
      throwing on every delegated access check -- a total fail-closed outage on the intended dev end-state.
      DataverseWebApiService is a safe template only because it has no OBO path.

      FIX: decoupled. (1) _credential gated by Graph:ManagedIdentity:Enabled. (2) _cca built whenever OBO config
      exists, INDEPENDENT of the flag -- DefaultAzureCredential cannot perform an OBO exchange (ADR-028 A4) and the
      MI flag says nothing about delegated access. This is also exactly the seam task 020 needs, so task 022 does
      not inherit the entanglement. Added fail-fast validation naming the missing setting.

      SECOND ADR-038 FINDING, self-caught at the quality gate: the first seam test read private fields by
      REFLECTION = ban B8. Rewritten behavioural-only (8 tests, 0 reflection). A behavioural assertion of the
      credential TYPE is genuinely impossible here -- the class is fail-closed and swallows credential errors into
      AccessRights.None -- so the structural decoupling guard was DEFERRED TO TASK 060 as source analysis, the
      shape ADR-038 sanctions and which fails at the shape level rather than on one sampled config. Booked onto
      060 as a constraint + acceptance criterion, not assumed.

      PRE-EXISTING CI FAILURE RAISED, NOT ABSORBED: GodClassGuardTests FR-14 is red on DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs
      (2975 vs 2864) and ComposeEndpoints.cs (2755 vs 2651). Neither is in this task's diff; ComposeEndpoints.cs is
      byte-identical to origin/master, proving the gate is red independently of this branch. Both arrived via the
      master merge from #3b and compose-r7. Remedy is decompose-or-re-baseline-with-reason, and it belongs to the
      projects that caused the growth.

      METADATA CORRECTION: group A was misclassified parallel-safe -- 010 and 011 BOTH modify
      DataverseAccessDataSource.cs and would have collided as concurrent sub-agents. Now parallel-safe: false on
      both, group re-marked 010 -> 011 sequential.

      Publish 43.67 MB compressed incl. PDBs (unchanged); CVE clean; LayerDependencyTests FR-14 passes;
      Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj zero diff.

      Full record: notes/decisions/010-credential-gating.md
    </completion>
  </notes>
</task>
